WEBVTT

NOTE week03-clip1-next-token-generation
NOTE Narration read by an AI-generated voice.
NOTE The clip has its own caption along the bottom of the frame, so these cues
NOTE are placed near the top to keep the two from overlapping.

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.848 line:2 align:center
A decoder, like the one in GPT,

2
00:00:02.848 --> 00:00:09.356 line:2 align:center
writes text one token at a time from left
to right. Here the note so far reads:

3
00:00:09.356 --> 00:00:12.617 line:2 align:center
the patient denies chest.

4
00:00:12.817 --> 00:00:14.733 line:2 align:center
Given everything written so far,

5
00:00:14.733 --> 00:00:20.234 line:2 align:center
the decoder outputs a probability
for every token in its vocabulary.

6
00:00:20.234 --> 00:00:23.817 line:2 align:center
The numbers on screen are illustrative.

7
00:00:24.017 --> 00:00:29.195 line:2 align:center
Greedy decoding simply takes the most
likely token, so the model writes pain,

8
00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:33.483 line:2 align:center
with a probability of 0.62.

9
00:00:33.683 --> 00:00:36.840 line:2 align:center
The chosen token, pain,
is appended to the input.

10
00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:41.245 line:2 align:center
In step two, the decoder runs
again on the longer sequence

11
00:00:41.245 --> 00:00:44.150 line:2 align:center
and writes the next token: and.

12
00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:48.794 line:2 align:center
Each forward pass adds exactly
one token. In step three,

13
00:00:48.794 --> 00:00:55.150 line:2 align:center
the model runs once more and adds
dyspnea, meaning shortness of breath.

14
00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:58.587 line:2 align:center
Greedy decoding always
takes the top token.

15
00:00:58.587 --> 00:01:02.623 line:2 align:center
Sampling draws a token
according to the probabilities,

16
00:01:02.623 --> 00:01:07.811 line:2 align:center
and the temperature controls how random
that draw is: low is nearly greedy,

17
00:01:07.811 --> 00:01:10.513 line:2 align:center
high is more varied.
